+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

HTTPS requests to private prediction endpoints verify the certificate
chain and the endpoint's DNS name or IP address. The port removes implicit
verification bypasses, including authenticated Private Service Connect
requests. A private network does not establish a TLS peer's identity.

Configure a trusted CA and use an endpoint name present in its certificate.
Requests-based PSC sessions honor REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE; urllib3-based private
endpoint requests use the Python SSL default trust configuration, including
SSL_CERT_FILE and SSL_CERT_DIR. Self-signed or mismatched certificates are
rejected. Endpoints explicitly using HTTP remain unencrypted.
